summary:
The supplier side has 3 nav tabs (My requests, Tasks, Help; catalog.ts:431-456) and one request page (SupplierCase) whose body changes with the phase. The live portal (src/portal) adds Notices and Corrections tabs.

Main findings:
1. **Duplicates.** My requests (SupplierHome) and Tasks (SupplierTasks) list the same work twice, and the Tasks "With Beiersdorf" and "Done" tabs repeat what the request page's "Questions for you" card and the home groups already show. Merge Tasks into My requests. Keep the SupplierTasks component, because the live portal's own nav still uses it.
2. **Stale content:**
   - the AS-06 "to be confirmed" text (ConfigQuestions.tsx:42);
   - the disabled "Download PDF" with "PDF generation not simulated" (PhaseViews.tsx:232-235), which AS-12/R-2 make stale;
   - the Help FAQ pointing to a Corrections tab the prototype doesn't have (SupplierHelp.tsx:83);
   - the video-guide DemoNote (SupplierHelp.tsx:186-206);
   - "In this prototype every invited contact may confirm" (Completeness.tsx:183);
   - document "version" wording and chips (FieldRenderer.tsx:91,137; AnswerDrawer.tsx:144,167), which BRM v2 REQ-PROC-016/-029 contradict (no versioning: documents are added with an upload date, no delete).
3. **Edge-case gaps that must be fixed:**
   - The final release isn't blocked while a question is open or in progress, or while required items are missing (FinalReleaseView, PhaseViews.tsx:156; app-plan-v4 D27). A completed reviewer can raise a question in final-release without the case going back to review (actions.ts:407).
   - Edits during final-release have no consequence (actions.ts:238-247), against AS-03 ("a completed review is reopened on change").
   - Closed requests lose the question history (SupplierCase.tsx:108-119 does not render QuestionsForYou), and nothing records the supplier's own confirmations.
   - Withdrawn questions disappear silently (PhaseViews.tsx:83). AS-08 question edits and closes by the raiser have no supplier view.
   - The supplier scope is per company, not per case contact (lib.ts:17-23, selectors.ts:214).
   - The supplier personas are hard-wired to two contacts (catalog.ts:431-456), so suppliers added in the demo can't be shown.
4. **Missing entirely:** the per-person simulated e-mail inbox (R-1, AS-08: mails on raise, return, edit and close, plus the invitation, the single release request, cancellation and reactivation), and a post-release "Report a change" path.
5. **Empty start:** with no cases, the supplier lands on three zero count tiles above a "No requests yet" card, and is greeted "Welcome back". Show only the empty state.
6. **Live portal (liveScope unset) must keep working:**
   - keep MetadataStep, ScopeCheckView, the old STEPS and the SupplierTasks component;
   - keep the AnswerDrawer "Upload a document" mode;
   - keep the harness strings ("Confirm completeness", "Confirm and submit", "Completeness confirmed", "Answer", "Upload a document", "Send to Beiersdorf", "How it works", "Your Beiersdorf contacts", no "Video guide");
   - gate every new behaviour with isLiveScope(c) where the live data differs.

items.details:
My requests becomes the single list: one card per request, ordered: action first (by earliest due), then with Beiersdorf, then closed. An active card lists its open tasks as rows inside it (REQ-PROC-030: one row per task):
- 'Fill in the CIQ and confirm completeness' with % done;
- each open question, with kind, ref.label, 'Asked by <name>, Beiersdorf', due date (DueText) and an 'Answer' button that opens the AnswerDrawer in place;
- 'Give the final release'.
The 'With Beiersdorf' and 'Done' tab content is not repeated here: answered or closed questions and the confirmations live on the request page (SUP-09, SUP-23). Remove the three CountTiles (SupplierHome.tsx:36-40), or keep one compact line ('2 requests in progress · 1 overdue') only when there are cases.

Keep as is, apart from SUP-16. Edge cases to keep:
- a CAS/EC check digit is wrong;
- min is greater than max;
- the concentration sum is below 100 or above 100 (hint only, never blocking);
- a value above the BDF limit asks for a justification;
- 'Cannot provide? Add a justification' counts as answered;
- GEN shows 'Pre-filled by Beiersdorf';
- an origin select limited to the SF-01 answers.
Two contacts editing the same K2.1 table: last write wins (E-D-97). This can't be shown in one browser; note it in the demo guide.

Must show:
- each answer, upload and justification with 'Answered by <name> (you)' and the time;
- the colleague hint on the completeness card;
- either contact can confirm or release, and the other then sees the new phase, with the release record naming who did it;
- both receive every supplier mail (SUP-27);
- a question answered by A shows 'With Beiersdorf' for B, with A's answer in the thread;
- a draft open in B's drawer when A already answered: B sees the 'With Beiersdorf' state (op.status in-progress) and no composer.

Add:
- finalRelease refused with an open or in-progress question and with blockers;
- a supplier change in final-release mails the affected reviewers, and reopening returns the case to review with a withdrawal mail;
- mails per event go to both contacts and never include a department completion, internal note, finding id or cancellation reason;
- an AS-08 edit and close produce supplier-visible messages; a withdrawn point stays listed;
- per-contact scope hides cases where the contact is not on supplierContactIds;
- the empty seed has 1 supplier, its contacts and 0 cases (update seed.test.ts expectations; seeded-case tests move to a fixture builder);
- release record content.
Keep the old-flow assertions (lib.test.ts:10-11 'portal' variant).
